# cvvdp_loop_smoke_2026-05-24.tsv — Phase 4 smoke bench meta

## Provenance

- **Chunk**: cvvdp-fork Phase 4 (`docs/RFC_CVVDP_PHASE4_BRIEF.md`, Step 5)
- **Date**: 2026-05-24
- **Encoder branch**: `cvvdp-fork-rfc` (stacked on parent Phase 3 `9c1cfa3e`)
- **Workspace**: `~/work/zen/jxl-encoder--cvvdp-loop-wiring`
- **Reproducer**: `examples/cvvdp_loop_smoke_bench.rs`
- **Run command**:
  ```bash
  cargo run --release -p jxl-encoder \
    --features "__expert butteraugli-loop cvvdp-loop ssim2-loop parallel" \
    --example cvvdp_loop_smoke_bench -- \
    --out benchmarks/cvvdp_loop_smoke_2026-05-24.tsv
  ```

## Schema

TSV header (RFC `docs/RFC_CVVDP_FORK.md` §5.3 master tracking schema):

| col | type | meaning |
|---|---|---|
| `image` | str | fixture name (see Fixtures below) |
| `corpus` | str | `synthetic` for all rows |
| `effort` | int | encoder effort (= 8; see Effort below) |
| `distance` | f32 | butteraugli `target_distance` |
| `backend` | str | `B` (CPU butteraugli baseline) or `C_GPU` (cvvdp opt-in) |
| `bytes` | int | encoded JXL size |
| `wall_ms` | f32 | encode wall time (rough — best-of-one, no rep stats) |
| `score_butter_cpu` | str | `NA` for this smoke bench (Phase 6 scores all metrics) |
| `score_butter_gpu` | str | `NA` |
| `score_cvvdp_gpu` | str | `NA` |
| `score_cvvdp_cpu` | str | `NA` |
| `score_ssim2` | str | `NA` |
| `notes` | str | `encoder_sha=<short> smoke_phase4 [cvvdp_loop=Some(true)]` |

## Fixtures

5 synthetic miniatures (self-contained — no codec-corpus dep so the
smoke bench runs anywhere):

- `gradient_64`: 64×64 RGB R=x G=y B=128
- `diagonal_128`: 128×128 RGB diagonal stripes (mid-frequency, exercises
  AC strategy refinement)
- `noisy_96`: 96×96 RGB radial brightness + high-frequency dithering
  (photo-like statistics)
- `flat_grey_32`: 32×32 RGB grey=128 (degenerate fixture — the buttloop
  has nothing to refine; included as a control)
- `checker_64`: 64×64 RGB 8×8 checker (high-contrast edges)

## Distances

`{0.5, 1.0, 2.0, 3.0}` — covers the butteraugli "very low" through
"high" bands per the CVVDP_DISTANCE_TARGETS lookup table.

## Effort

`effort = 8`. The buttloop gates at `speed_tier <= kKitten`
(`enc_adaptive_quantization.cc:1282`), which is `effort >= 8` in our
mapping. At effort 7 (production Zenjxl default for many cells) the
buttloop never invokes `compare_with_reference`, so the cvvdp opt-in
would be a no-op and every cell would be byte-identical. Effort 8
forces the buttloop to engage so the smoke bench exercises the Phase 4
plumbing path.

## Observations from this run

- **CVVDP fires and changes bytes**: 16 of 20 cells show non-zero
  Δbytes (the cvvdp-driven loop converges to a different quant_field
  than butteraugli, as expected from the score-direction mapping +
  1.05× tightened JOD target).
- **C_GPU > B bytes on every non-degenerate cell**: the cvvdp target
  table is more conservative than butteraugli's natural convergence at
  the same nominal `target_distance`. Photo-like + text-like content
  shows the largest deltas (noisy_96 d=3.0: +386%; diagonal_128 d=3.0:
  +262%; checker_64 d=2.0: +104%). This is the Phase 4 expected
  behaviour — the 1.05× tighter target translates to substantially
  more bytes on content where cvvdp scores the butteraugli baseline
  as "perceptually inadequate."
- **Degenerate fixture (flat_grey_32) ≈ unchanged**: Δbytes within
  ±5% across all 4 distances — flat content has nothing for the
  perceptual metric to differentiate, so the loop converges to the
  same outcome on both backends.
- **Wall time**: C_GPU is slower (~2-10× the butteraugli baseline at
  these tiny sizes) because the GPU compute kernel has fixed per-iter
  overhead (CUDA launch + small-image scheduling) that dominates at
  ≤128² sizes. The Phase 6 sweep on real CID22 + GB82-SC images will
  show the GPU asymptote where the kernel speedup vs CPU butteraugli
  matters; this smoke bench is sized to validate plumbing not perf.

## What this bench is NOT

- **Not a Pareto judgement.** Bigger files at the same nominal
  distance does NOT mean cvvdp is "worse" — it means it's calibrated
  differently. Phase 6 (RFC §5.4) is where SSIM2 / cvvdp / butteraugli
  scores are jointly weighed against bytes to make the
  default-flip / RD decision.
- **Not a perf bench.** 1-run-best-of-1 wall_ms on synthetic
  miniatures isn't representative of production-image throughput.
- **Not a JOD calibration validation.** The CVVDP_DISTANCE_TARGETS
  table was seeded from Agent D's 1,131-cell butteraugli baseline +
  1.05× tightening. Phase 6 will re-validate / rebake the table from
  a wider sweep against the post-Phase-4 encoder output.

## Where this lands in the master tracking TSV

This 40-row file (20 cells × {B, C_GPU} = 40 rows) supplements (does
NOT replace) the master `benchmarks/cvvdp_vs_buttloop_tracking_2026-05-24.tsv`
which carries the Agent D 1,131-cell butteraugli-baseline rows. The
master TSV will get a fresh full-sweep refresh in Phase 6 (per RFC
§5.4) with the post-Phase-4 encoder, including the `C_GPU` rows the
smoke bench prototypes here.

